
Run the audio_utility.py and then figureout the input and output audio device
Then update that information in config.py

Create a virtual env
|----- python -m venv .venv


Start the virtual env:
|
|------Windows:
|        .venv\Scripts\activate
|------Linux:
|        source .venv/bin/activate


Export dependencies:
|
|----- pip freeze > requirements.txt

Install dependencies:
|
|----- pip install -r requirements.txt

On the new system:
|
|--- python -m venv .venv
|--- source .venv/bin/activate   # or .venv\Scripts\activate on Windows
|--- pip install -r requirements.txt


File descriptions:
|
|----- config.py // Configuration constants! 
|----- main.py //  Main entry point of the program!
|----- audio_processing.py // Audio capture and feature extraction.
|----- model_engine.py // Loads and runs ML model.
|----- input_handler.py // Detects keypress and exits the app.


